			],
			"Message": "docs(Echo): Restructure README with tagline hook, architecture tables, and streamlined sections\n\nReplace verbose introductory paragraphs with a punchy blockquote tagline that immediately contrasts Echo against `tokio::spawn`. Restructure the Overview into four clear engineered goals. Remove redundant standalone sections (Call for Contributions, License, Changelog, Project Maintainers) whose content already lives under standard ecosystem links.\n\nKey changes:\n- Replace the multi-paragraph blurb with a tagline blockquote + quoted value proposition\n- Rewrite Overview as a bold elevator pitch plus numbered goals (Prioritize, Maximize, Structure, Decouple)\n- Expand Key Features with a new \"Lock-Free Performance\" entry and bolder headings\n- Replace the old Architecture Principles table with a richer cross-referenced version (Principle, Description, Key Components)\n- Add emoji-decorated labels to the Mermaid diagram nodes and append a Connection Paths table after the diagram\n- Expand Key Components table from 4 to 9 rows covering every individual source file\n- Add a new Project Structure ASCII tree showing Source/ and Documentation/ layout\n- Add a Layer integration table to the In the Land Project section (Mountain/Echo/Common)\n- Add Prerequisites subsection and update installation example to use Land workspace URL\n- Simplify the Funding section table by removing the HTML header row; add NLnet grant agreement number\n- Normalize URLs: `Rust.Documentation.editor.land` to `rust.documentation.echo.editor.land`, `editor.land` to `Editor.Land`\n\nThe result is a more scannable, developer-friendly README that immediately communicates Echo's value proposition and architectural role within the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "813e02b2728db64c43cdac7b82aba91ac8594054"
		},
